---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';

const title = 'About | WhatChar';
const description = 'Learn what WhatChar does and why confusing Unicode characters, homoglyphs, and invisible spaces matter.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang="en" locale="en" path="/about/">
  <header class="topbar">
    <Brand />
  </header>

  <main class="page-shell">
    <section class="seo-copy legal-page">
      <h1>About WhatChar</h1>

      <p>
        WhatChar is a small browser-based tool for checking confusing Unicode characters.
        It helps identify characters that look similar, such as lowercase l, uppercase I,
        digit 1, Latin O, digit 0, Greek and Cyrillic lookalikes, Hangul lookalikes,
        fullwidth forms, punctuation variants, and invisible spaces.
      </p>

      <p>
        The tool is designed for people who need to inspect suspicious text, usernames,
        domains, code snippets, social media posts, or copied text where visually similar
        characters may be confusing.
      </p>

      <p>
        All analysis runs locally in your browser. The text you paste is not sent to a server.
      </p>

      <h2>Part of Kakerio</h2>

      <p>
        WhatChar is a tool by <a href="https://kakerio.com/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kakerio</a>,
        a family of small browser tools for text and CSV files. It keeps its own address,
        isitiorl.com, and works exactly as before.
      </p>

      <p>
        If the text you are checking also has other problems, these Kakerio tools may help:
        <a href="https://kakerio.com/en/tools/text-normalizer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Japanese Text Normalizer</a>
        for full-width, half-width and kana forms,
        <a href="https://kakerio.com/en/tools/mojibake-fixer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mojibake Fixer</a>
        for garbled text, and
        <a href="https://kakerio.com/en/tools/csv-doctor/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CSV Doctor</a>
        for CSV files. Like WhatChar, they process your text in your browser.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <span><a href="/">Home</a></span>
    <span><a href="/contact/">Contact</a></span>
    <span><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a></span>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>